<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="1">
<Content>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
<Text>INT. NIKE OUTLET STORE - MORNING</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action">
<Text>JORDAN PARK, 30s, laces up a pair of clearance running shoes under a wall sized Nike swoosh, checking the price tag twice before deciding it's worth it.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>JORDAN</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>Sold. Ring it up.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
<Text>EXT. GOLDEN GATE BRIDGE - DAWN</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action">
<Text>Jordan runs the span alone, breath fogging in the cold. The city is still asleep behind her.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>JORDAN</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>(breathless, to no one)</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>Bet even presidents get winded up here. They say Barack Obama used to run this exact stretch, back before the motorcade got too big for it.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
<Text>INT. DOWNTOWN COFFEE SHOP - LATER</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action">
<Text>Jordan orders at the counter. A flyer on the corkboard advertises an opening at the fictional local firm VELLUM &amp; ASH ACCOUNTING.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>JORDAN</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>One coffee, whatever's fastest. I've got that interview in ten minutes.</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character">
<Text>BARISTA</Text>
</Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
<Text>Big day. Good luck.</Text>
</Paragraph>
</Content>
</FinalDraft>
